Z||000000||fierospeeder||05-07-2001||05:14 PM||||Dear Mr. Kosik,<P>Thank you for contacting the Internet Response Center.  We certainly appreciate your interest and <BR>enthusiasm for the Pontiac Fiero.  Contrary to rumors that seem have have spread, GM did not destroy<BR>the prototype 1989 Fiero.  This model will continue to be stored, along with all the other <BR>prototypes and concept vehicles, at the GM Proving Ground facility in Michigan.  Unfortunately, body<BR>kits would not be available and it is unlikely that Pontiac would ever produce them.<P>Thank you again for contacting the Internet Response Center and for making Pontiac your vehicle of <BR>choice.  <P>Sincerely,<P>Donald Stailey<BR>Customer Relationship Manager<BR>GM Internet Response Center<BR>||||reg||10
